# Hackathon Submission Draft - ResearchPilot AI

**Project name:** ResearchPilot AI
**Track:** Best Apps and Agents
**Tagline:** From scattered information to evidence-backed intelligence.

## Elevator pitch
ResearchPilot AI is a research agent that doesn't just answer - it shows its evidence. It plans a research strategy,
searches the live web and your own PDFs, and produces a cited report in which every claim points to a real source,
and gaps are called out instead of papered over.

## Problem
Chatbot answers to research questions are fluent but unverifiable. Students and developers waste time checking
claims, and fabricated citations are a real risk.

## Target users
University students, developers evaluating technologies, AI/ML learners, and researchers synthesising sources.

## Solution and unique value
- Separates **evidence** (tool outputs) from **interpretation** (model text).
- Citation IDs are assigned by code; invented citations are detected and removed.
- Bounded agent (tool-call, round and time limits) with a real activity timeline.
- Works on web sources, uploaded documents, or both; says "no evidence" rather than guessing.
- Project memory the user fully controls, and a downloadable Markdown report with a methodology section that reflects what actually ran.

## Key features
Research planning · Tavily web search · PDF/TXT/MD RAG with page attribution · SQLite project memory ·
Markdown report export · explainable activity timeline · prompt-injection-aware evidence handling.

## Technology stack
Python, Streamlit, FAISS, PyMuPDF, SQLite, `requests`, pytest/unittest.

## NVIDIA model
Default: **`nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B`** (configurable via `NEBIUS_MODEL`).
